# pin-action-shas-to-commit --- History

## v2.0.0 (2026-03-25)

**Changed by:** ProjectScylla issue #1534 -- full repo-wide SHA pinning with regression tests
**Verification:** verified-local

### What changed
- Expanded scope from composite actions only to ALL workflow + composite action files
- Added regression test pattern (pytest parametrized over .github/ YAML files)
- Added batch SHA resolution script for multiple actions
- Added 6 new verified SHAs (actions/checkout, cache, upload-artifact, codecov, trivy-action)
- Added "Verified On" entry for ProjectScylla
- Updated verification commands to cover bare semver tags (e.g. @0.35.0) not just v-tags

### Why
v1.0.0 focused only on composite action files that were missed in an initial pinning pass.
Issue #1534 required a full repo-wide pinning of all 16 external references across 7 files,
including workflow files. The regression test pattern prevents future regressions when new
actions are added.

### Previous version (v1.0.0) snapshot

```yaml
---
name: pin-action-shas-to-commit
description: 'Pin GitHub Actions version tags to full commit SHAs for supply chain
  security. Use when: composite action files use mutable tags like @v8 or @v0.9.4
  instead of full 40-char commit SHAs.'
category: ci-cd
date: 2026-03-07
version: 1.0.0
user-invocable: false
---
```

Covered: composite actions only (.github/actions/), 2 verified SHAs (prefix-dev/setup-pixi, actions/github-script).
Did not include: workflow files, regression tests, batch resolution, bare semver tag detection.

